    <description>After-save on AF_CreditNote__c, paired with the before-save AF_FL_CreditNote_SetApprovalStatus. Submits the record into AF_AP_CreditNote_Cancellation only on the transition into Pending, never on a later unrelated save while already Pending, since re-submitting an in-flight approval request errors.

LFRDN-729 fix: previously fired for AF_Reason__c = Cancellation too, submitting the refund credit note the instant it was created - fully independent of, and racing ahead of, the Opportunity&apos;s own cancellation approval (AF_AP_Opp_Cancellation). A rejected cancellation left its refund Pending forever, and a second cancellation request created a second, duplicate Pending refund. Restricted this criteria to AF_Reason__c != Cancellation - cancellation refunds are now only ever submitted by AF_CreditNote_CancellationLinkService, called from AF_FL_Opp_AfterCancellationApprovalOutcome once the Opportunity&apos;s own cancellation approval is actually Approved. Non-cancellation credit notes (e.g. AF_Reason__c = Customer Request) are unaffected and still submit immediately as before.

LFRDN-761 (2026-09-28): AF_AP_CreditNote_Cancellation routes to the Owner&apos;s Manager, but AF_CreditNote__c and Opportunity are Private and the Manager may sit outside the deal&apos;s business unit. Cancellation refunds already get the share in AF_CreditNote_CancellationLinkService; this path (every other credit note) now does the same before submitting: AF_CreditNote__Share and OpportunityShare, Edit/Manual, for the Owner&apos;s Manager.</description>
